16. What Happens When Work Moves Into Planning

This is a core requirement.

When a task moves from Wishlist into Planning:

1. Detect the change.
2. Identify the owner.
3. Read Start Date.
4. Read Due Date.
5. Read Estimated Effort.
6. Allocate the effort across the appropriate weeks.
7. Recalculate that person’s utilisation.
8. Recalculate team utilisation.
9. Determine whether any week crosses a capacity threshold.
10. Update the dashboard.

If the new work causes someone to move into:

STRETCHED

or

OVER CAPACITY

flag this prominently.

Example:

Capacity Warning

Recruitment Dashboard has been added to Planning.

Person A’s utilisation for week commencing 12 October changes:

Before: 89%
After: 112%

Status: OVER CAPACITY

Additional demand: 3 days

The dashboard should clearly identify the newly added piece of work as the cause.

